</applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>WACHI, SHUN</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>FURUKAWA NAOKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TERAZAWA HIROMU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>WACHI SHUN</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>FURUKAWA, NAOKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TERAZAWA, HIROMU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>WACHI, SHUN</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A polymerization initiator, a cationically polymerizable monomer ingredient, and a catalyst are continuously fed to a flow-through stirring vessel type reactor to initiate living polymerization and, simultaneously therewith, the reaction mixture in which the conversion of the cationically polymerization monomer ingredient has reached a value of from 1 wt.% to less than 90 wt.% is continuously fed from the flow-through stirring vessel type reactor to a flow-through tubular reactor to cause the living polymerization to proceed further. Thus, a polymer is produced.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>Un amorceur de polymérisation, un ingrédient monomère polymérisable de manière cationique et un catalyseur sont introduits en continu dans un réacteur de type cuve d'agitation à circulation continue, de manière à déclencher une polymérisation vivante et, simultanément, le mélange réactionnel dans lequel la conversion de l'ingrédient monomère polymérisable de manière cationique a atteint une valeur comprise entre 1 % en poids et 90 % en poids est transféré en continu du réacteur de type cuve d'agitation à circulation continue vers un réacteur tubulaire à circulation continue de sorte que la polymérisation puisse se poursuivre. Il est ainsi produit un polymère.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>